`ErrorBoundary.tsx` created. Usage:

```tsx
// Default fallback
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary fallback={(error, reset) => (
  <div>
    <p>{error.message}</p>
    <button onClick={reset}>Try again</button>
  </div>
)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key details:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error into state to trigger the fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` logs `error.message`, `stack`, and `componentStack` to the console
- `reset()` clears state, remounting children — this is the retry mechanism
- `fallback` prop lets callers supply custom UI; default UI is a styled `role="alert"` div
